A1. This runs up and down the street and all around the town. ~ CURB
A5. A great composer. ~ SLEEP
A10. An alarming feature of the present time to the rising generation. ~ BELL
A14. This is bitter medicine. ~ ALOE
A15. The conclusion of a fable. ~ MORAL
A16. This has a bank in Canada and also in New York. ~ ERIE
A17. This is a hindrance. ~ SNAG
A18. Conscious. ~ AWARE
A19. These embrace many forms. ~ ARMS
A20. This holds a high flier. ~ HANGAR
A22. What a sentence from the "Judge" does. ~ AMUSES
A24. Winter quarters for golf clubs. ~ ATTIC
A27. This goes with a dash. ~ DOT
A28. What Dad has to do with his clothes when son comes home from college. ~ SHARE
A31. This fellow doesn't amount to much. ~ CAD
A33. This is what a shrinking maiden might become. ~ SYLPH
A37. A beach coat. ~ TAN
A38. There is a difference of opinion here. ~ DEBATE
A40. Form of verb "to be." ~ ARE
A41. To vex. ~ IRK
A42. These are fine for reducing. ~ FAMINES
A43. This one has been in the tanning business for years. ~ SOL
A44. This is rather fishy. ~ EEL
A45. This one was skinned down in Florida last year. ~ ORANGE
A46. When you get this, your problem is solved. ~ SUM
A47. This comes from the Chicago Stock Yards. ~ SMELL
A49. Born. ~ NEE
